From: NanoKVM build <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] configs: licheerv_nano: raise kernel/fdt/script load addresses

The default kernel_addr_r=0x81000000 sits only 14 MiB above SDRAM base.
This build boots a FIT (boot.sd) whose kernel has load address 0x80200000
and is ~28 MiB, so the kernel's destination (0x80200000..~0x81E00000)
overlaps the FIT staged at kernel_addr_r, and bootm aborts:
"new format image overwritten - must RESET the board to recover".
Move the FIT/fdt/script staging above the kernel run region (256 MiB DRAM,
base 0x80000000): kernel_addr_r=0x84000000, fdt_addr_r=0x88000000,
scriptaddr=0x83000000. The kernel itself still runs at 0x80200000.
---
diff --git a/include/configs/licheerv_nano.h b/include/configs/licheerv_nano.h
index 2ea7943..4c81e2b 100644
--- a/include/configs/licheerv_nano.h
+++ b/include/configs/licheerv_nano.h
@@ -16,9 +16,9 @@
 
 #define CFG_EXTRA_ENV_SETTINGS  "consoledev=ttyS0\0" \
 								"baudrate=115200\0" \
-								"fdt_addr_r=0x82000000\0" \
-								"kernel_addr_r=0x81000000\0" \
-								"scriptaddr=0x80c00000\0" \
+								"fdt_addr_r=0x88000000\0" \
+								"kernel_addr_r=0x84000000\0" \
+								"scriptaddr=0x83000000\0" \
 								BOOTENV
 
 #endif /* __CONFIG_H */
